 "text": "Hello there! How's everything with you? I usually say them out loud on Friday afternoons while I' walking out to the car. It' a good way to start the weekend. Then think about what you'd like to do then. A picnic by the river, a concert, something special. Most people still get paper bills, so a mix of phone call and letter is reliable. Email is great too, it shows they' online. Nice. A simple design, with the months across the top and a space for a personal note on the back, would be lovely. She'd be proud of her handywork. I still use a dodgy ballpoint that runs bit and leaves a blurry trail. It feels like old home weekends.",
